<section id="safety" class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Safety in the recorded trajectories</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="report-prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Exploration and recovery also expose safety weaknesses.</strong> Failed dishwasher
        and apple-to-bowl episodes show objects slipping from the gripper, followed by repeated arm
        and base repositioning to search for them. During exploration, the agent also attempts
        motions beyond the robot’s workspace. The coffee-bean case reveals a further problem:
        awkward EEF poses and insufficient attention to object–scene contact. Together, these
        failures highlight the need to preserve grasp stability, enforce workspace constraints and
        account for contact throughout manipulation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="behavior-tabs safety-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Safety evidence">
      <button
        id="safety-tab-dishwasher"
        data-safety="dishwasher"
        role="tab"
        aria-controls="safety-content"
        aria-selected="true"
      >
        Dishwasher · dropped bowl
      </button>
      <button
        id="safety-tab-apple"
        data-safety="apple"
        role="tab"
        aria-controls="safety-content"
        aria-selected="false"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        Apple · workspace limits
      </button>
      <button
        id="safety-tab-coffee"
        data-safety="coffee"
        role="tab"
        aria-controls="safety-content"
        aria-selected="false"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        Coffee beans · posture And contact
      </button>
    </div>
    <div
      id="safety-content"
      role="tabpanel"
      aria-labelledby="safety-tab-dishwasher"
      tabindex="0"
    ></div>
  </div>
</section>
